+## Mention Autocomplete & Webhooks
+- Bots appear in the @-mention autocomplete dropdown in the message editor, identical to normal members.
+- Whenever a user mentions an active bot in a room, the bot's webhook URL is triggered asynchronously (never blocking message creation or delivery).
+- Webhook Payload (`Content-Type: application/json`):
+```json
+{
+  "event": "mention",
+  "author": { "id": 7, "name": "Alice" },
+  "room": { "id": 5, "name": "Ops", "reply_to": "/rooms/5/42-Xy3abc9defGh/messages" },
+  "message": {
+    "id": 118,
+    "body": {
+      "text": "restart the build please",
+      "html": "<div>… full rich-text body …</div>"
+    },
+    "link": "/rooms/5/@118"
+  }
+}
+```
+- `message.body.text` has the bot's own @-mention stripped so the text reads as the command directed at the bot.
+- `room.reply_to` provides the bot's posting endpoint to respond out-of-band.
+- The bot can reply:
+  - Synchronously with HTTP 200 and `Content-Type: text/plain` or `text/html` (response body is posted to the room as the bot).
+  - Synchronously with HTTP 204 (no message posted).
+  - Asynchronously later by sending a POST request to `room.reply_to`.
+
